{
  "schema": "varve.agent-parity/1",
  "updated": "2026-10-15",
  "notes": [
    "Machine-readable parity manifest for the automation command surface.",
    "Denominators are real: `inventoryAtCapture` is the action ids the editor actually dispatches, enumerated from createActionHandlers, not a menu count.",
    "A new action id must be classified as `reviewed` (it has a semantic command) or `notACommand` (with a reason from the closed set) before the gate passes. Adding it to neither fails the check.",
    "`unmappedBacklog` is the recorded debt: the UI can do it and no semantic command exists yet. It carries one expiry so the debt cannot become permanent by default.",
    "Only `reviewed` is enforced. `commands[].uiSurfaces` is informational: inspector edits (for example opacity on a slider) reach the document through a direct call and have no dispatcher action id, so they can never appear in `reviewed`."
  ],
